    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Cardinality of a Finite Set",
    "problem": "If $C={♣,♠,♡,♢,△,♣}$, then $|C|=$",
    "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $C$ is the number of elements in $C.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $C:$\n\n$$\n♣,\\,♠,\\,♡,\\,♢,\\,△\n$$\n\nNote that only *unique* elements are counted. In other words, duplicate elements are *not* counted separately.\n\nSince $C$ has $5$ elements, its cardinality is $|C|=5.$",
